      {
        "review_id": 241866015,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r241866015-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "One of the Holiest Temples - Outstanding!",
        "text": "We paid a memorable visit to the area around Lord Shiva's Pashupati Temple on the banks of the Bagmati River.  Even several streets away, we could feel the religious fervor of the people who throng here.  We saw Linga stones in the street where the puja was recently performed.  We saw people with bare feet performing rituals; further on we saw holy men resting on the Ghats; and we saw many cremations on the Ghats at the river bank.  I was fascinated at the spectacle of it all...the shouts and chants; the mourners' cries; the scent of burning sandalwood; the exoticism of the site.  Cows and goats and monkeys run free as they do in other parts of Nepal.\n\nThough non-Hindu visitors to the temple are not allowed, we saw much and experienced rituals and religious ceremonies that Westerners don't normally see.  The golden roofs of the temple can be seen from many vantage points and the mountains rise high above all of this.  The place is magical and must be experienced by any and all who come to Nepal.",
