      {
        "review_id": 241530676,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r241530676-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Majestic !",
        "text": "The Pashupati Nath Temple , Amongst the holiest shrine for Hindus, is dedicated to Lord Shiva is located at the banks of river Baghmati. It takes 20-25 minutes considering the traffic from Airport and City Centre to reach here. \nYou may only take darshan or you may perform a special Pooja called \" Pinda Dana\" or offerings to your forefathers. I performed one which took roughy an hour at the hands of a Brahman who typically takes Rs 2500 ( Nepali) for this pooja. He gets all the material required for the pooja included in this cost. This kind of Pooja is done only at Tyrambakeshwar ( Nasik, Maharashtra) and Gaya ( Bihar, India) and Pashupatinath.\nWhen you enter the temple you will see a huge Nandi ( Sacred bull and carrier of Lord Shiva) offered to the temple by the King of Nepal. Lord Shiva as Pashupatinath has Five heads and hence there are four gates to the temple for each direction. The fifth head is on the top of the Linga. You have to take darshan visiting each gate one by one. \nAarti of River Baghmati is performed as of Mother Ganga in Benaras, India. Its a treat to watch. It is performed at sunset. Please check for time difference in Nepal as Nepalese time is 15 minutes ahead of Indian time.\nOverall its a deeply spiritual expreience to be at one of the holiest shrines of Hindu Religion. \nMust go in a life time!",
        "review_tip": null,
