      {
        "review_id": 241354752,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r241354752-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A must experience",
        "text": "A must experience for the Hindus who want to get darshan. But also the non-Hindus can watch the cremations and the sunset aarti. Its a great photo opportunity if not anything else! Loads of monkeys around chilling, just doing their thing. Lots of Holy men as well, cant make out if they are real or not but they will pose for photos for money :)\n\nIf you want to go inside for Darshan you have to deposit your shoes and bag/camera in the locker provided. If not then u can keep your shoes and camera and just go directly for watching the aarti. \n\nThe architecture is lovely and its close to the Bagmati river. Watching the cremation is definitely eye opening. Once dead we are just a body after all.",
