      {
        "review_id": 241112299,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r241112299-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Quite an experience",
        "text": "Although there is, what feels like a hefty price of 1000rs (about £10) entrance fee, this museum complex was an amazing experience. On arrival, there was no clear signs as to what part of the temple complex non-Hindus could enter and we ended up being told off by two people when we tried to enter a building. At first we thought it was because we had our shoes on still, but a kind woman told us that the area was for Hindus only. At first we thought we had paid to just stand in a courtyard, but after walking around we realised that we were to go behind the temple. This is where the cremations were happening. After exploring the rest of the complex, we sat on the opposite side of the river and watched a cremation ceremony. It sounds morbid but the actually experience was moving and sincere. We watch a family walked around the pyre and conduct various rituals before it was lit. Yes tourist were taking photos, but they were respectful of the family and were quite quiet during the ceremony. Certainly an experience. \nAlso, this place had more monkeys than the so-called 'Monkey Temple'!",
        "review_tip": null,
